# PART 21: DEVELOPMENT EXECUTION RULES

These requirements are mandatory.

1. First inspect the supplied brand assets and existing project files.

2. Establish the global design system before building individual screens.

3. Build the reusable application shell and navigation.

4. Develop the application in logical modules.

5. Preserve existing working functionality when modifying the project.

6. Do not generate a static mock-up.

7. Do not leave important buttons non-functional.

8. Do not use placeholder links that lead nowhere.

9. Do not create duplicate pages with slightly different styling.

10. Maintain consistent design tokens and reusable components.

11. Do not invent real payment integrations or authentication services.

12. Do not fabricate real-world verification.

13. Use clear demonstration labels wherever sample data or simulated functionality is used.

14. Test the main user journeys after implementation.

15. Fix compilation errors and runtime errors before considering a feature complete.

16. Do not sacrifice mobile usability for desktop aesthetics.

17. Do not remove features simply because implementation is inconvenient.

18. If a feature cannot be fully implemented in the current prototype environment, implement the best honest demonstration possible and document what remains.

